<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patch>
	<!--
		USER-REQUESTED: bulk goods traders are the ONLY traders that buy toys.

		How: vanilla's buy-only stock generator (StockGenerator_BuyTradeTag
		generates no stock; it only makes the trader willing to BUY things
		carrying the tag, exactly like vanilla's Art / MusicalInstrument buyers).
		Every toy ThingDef carries the "Toys" trade tag (ThingDefs_Toys.xml).

		Which traders: every TraderKindDef whose defName contains "BulkGoods"
		(vanilla: Caravan_Outlander_BulkGoods, Caravan_Neolithic_BulkGoods,
		Orbital_BulkGoods; modded bulk traders that follow vanilla naming are
		picked up automatically). PatchOperationAdd targets the stockGenerators
		LIST node (patches lore) and applies to every match.

		Why nobody else buys them (verified against vanilla trader defs): no
		vanilla trader has a Category generator for "Toys" or any ancestor of it,
		nor a tag generator for "Toys"; the only generic catch-all buyer,
		StockGenerator_BuyExpensiveSimple (exotic traders), skips anything with
		genericMarketSellable = false, which every toy now sets. Plush toys are
		Apparel, which that buyer skips anyway.

		success=Always: if a mod removes or renames every bulk goods trader, this
		quietly does nothing instead of logging a patch failure.
	-->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
		<success>Always</success>
		<xpath>Defs/TraderKindDef[contains(defName, "BulkGoods")]/stockGenerators</xpath>
		<value>
			<li Class="StockGenerator_BuyTradeTag">
				<tag>Toys</tag>
			</li>
		</value>
	</Operation>
</Patch>
